{
  "dom_id": "step-q74351",
  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "The following table shows the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[1,7].$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2.5$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $5$ | $8.5$ | $9$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum, with the three subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[1,7].$",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈f(2.5)Δ{x}_{1}+f(5)Δ{x}_{2}+f(7)Δ{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2.5$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $-$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ | $2$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $5$ | $8.5$ | $9$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈5\\cdot 1.5+8.5\\cdot 2.5+9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =7.5+21.25+18 \\\\  & =46.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
